[All rectangular product polarizations]\label{thm:main}
For any positive integers $a,b,d$, a general smooth curve in $|N(3ad,3bd)|$ has relative stable Frobenius rank
\begin{equation}\label{eq:main}
 r_d=9abd^2-1-(1-f_2)\epsilon(ad)-(1-f_1)\epsilon(bd).
\end{equation}
Its genus is $9abd^2+1$ and its relative coherent dimension is $9abd^2-1$. There is no restriction on the ordinary elliptic parameter or on the $2$-adic valuations of $a,b,d$.

Over a perfect field the same assertion holds for geometric generic rank after algebraic closure. For the embedding defined by $L=N(3a,3b)$, formula \eqref{eq:main} holds for ambient degree-$d$ hypersurfaces whenever restriction onto $H^0(A,L^d)$ is surjective; a sufficient range is
\[
 d\ge\max\{1,\operatorname{reg}(\mathcal I_A)-1\}.
\]

[The even thin systems]\label{thm:thin}
Let $E_{\rm o}$ be any ordinary elliptic curve and $E_{\rm s}$ any supersingular elliptic curve over $k$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item For every even $m\ge6$, a general member of
$|\OO_{E_{\rm o}}(mO)\boxtimes\OO_{E_{\rm s}}(3O)|$ has genus $3m+1$, full $2$-rank $3m-1$, and relative rank $3m-2$.
\item For every even $m\ge6$, a general member of
$|\OO_{E_{\rm s}}(mO)\boxtimes\OO_{E_{\rm s}}(3O)|$ has genus $3m+1$ and full and relative rank $3m-2$. Proposition~\ref{prop:ss-all-even} gives an explicit section in every such degree. For $m=2q$ with $6\mid q$, Proposition~\ref{prop:ss-sparse} gives a second explicit family with first and second Cartier ranks $6q-2$.
\end{enumerate}

[A uniform sparse section]\label{prop:ss-sparse}
For every positive $q$ divisible by six, define a section of $N(2q,3)$ on $E\times E$ by
\begin{align*}
 s_q&=A+Bz+Cw,\qquad P=x^{q-3},\\
 A&=x+P\{x^2+(1+x)y\},\qquad B=x+Py^2,\qquad C=1+Py.
\end{align*}
Its first and second Cartier ranks are both $6q-2$. A general smooth member of $|N(2q,3)|$ therefore has full and relative stable rank $6q-2$.
